    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-20T15:55:36+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T15:55:36+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-20T06:25:36Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-20T06:25:36Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lies over the north of the state and moves northeastwards to clear the state on Friday. An another trough moves over the southeast Thursday evening. A high pressure system moves into the west on Friday and continues moving slowly eastwards to be situated in the Tasman Sea on Sunday. A low pressure system and associated trough move into the far west on Sunday and then moves across the state on Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-20T15:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-20T05:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light in the late afternoon.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Slight chance of a shower near the coast in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Light winds becoming south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the middle of the day then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 3 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 15 and 18.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:10am to 2:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-22T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-23T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-21T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-22T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Light winds. Overnight temperatures falling to between 2 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching between 15 and 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-23T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-24T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-22T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-23T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Light winds becoming north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then tending east to northeasterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 3 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-24T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-25T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-23T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-24T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of rain. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting south to southwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 14 and 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
